  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 128 AM EDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nA strong ridge pattern across the western US will continue to expand \nacross to even the southeastern US while surface high pressure \nremains parked over the Florida Peninsula. This pattern will prevent \ntroughing across most of the Eastern Seaboard from pushing further \nsouth, which is expected to keep the local weather primarily sea \nbreeze driven, although some vorticity advection from the upper-\nlevel low tracking across Cuba could provide extra support for \nshower and thunderstorm development on Friday as even deeper \nmoisture returns to the region. Highest rain chances would remain \nacross SW Florida as low level flow remains easterly around the \nridge. For the weekend time period, troughing becomes enhanced \nacross the Eastern Seaboard due to the strengthening ridge producing \na quasi-meriodional flow at jet stream level. Energy from this \ntrough could push far enough south for Sunday and into early next \nweek, but this still remains uncertain given it is near the end of \nthe forecast period. Regardless, after a brief lull in increased \nrain shower and thunderstorm activity, the pattern looks to become \nmore active over the next week.\n\nHigh temperatures each day will continue to reach the low to mid \n90s. Overnight lows will range from the low 70s for interior South \nFlorida to the upper 70s and low 80s near the Gulf and Atlantic \ncoasts. Potential for Heat Advisories will continue with each day \nassessed carefully due to most days being a marginal scenario.",
